TokenJoy modifications (2026-11-17): private authenticated bounded job API;
connection-time public-IP DNS pinning and TLS origin preservation; bounded
streaming, request/token limits, disabled HTTP/environment reference retries
and caches; strict report field/metrics allowlists; truthful signature label;
long-context opt-in and failure-stop; packaging, deployment docs and tests.
Additional TokenJoy modification (2026-11-17): authenticated transient catalog
lookup with the same secure outbound transport, fixed model-list request,
bounded filtered Claude/OpenAI/Gemini IDs and no inference probes or storage.
Catalog compatibility: prefer Bearer-only OpenAI format; one 401/403 native
authentication fallback and bounded same-origin cursor pagination, with a
GET-only fixed-path query allowlist and no partial catalog on budget exhaustion.
Fake-IP DNS compatibility: benchmark-only system answers may use one bounded
fixed public DoH lookup; connection-time public-IP and TLS validation remain.

